## 8. Assumptions
- Jira API simulator or sandbox is available for negative testing.
- Test credentials (valid/invalid/expired) are provisioned.
- Logging and monitoring access is enabled for test runs.

## 9. Risk Mitigation Table
Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Severity | Mitigation Action
---|---|---|---|---|---
R1 | Jira API authentication failures (401/403) block test coverage | High | High | Critical | Provision valid/invalid tokens, use API simulator for negative cases
R2 | Description field missing due to upstream permission issues | Medium | High | Major | Use mock payloads, verify fallback handling in consumer
R3 | Test data setup delays (credential provisioning) | Medium | Medium | Moderate | Pre-request all test credentials, escalate blockers to DevOps
R4 | Logging/monitoring not enabled for test runs | Low | Medium | Minor | Confirm logging config before execution, add test hooks
R5 | Timeline slippage due to environment unavailability | Medium | Medium | Major | Schedule environment slots in advance, use local mocks if blocked

